{
  "_what": "THE ONE PIN LIST: every scanner, linter and CLI the kit installs, by exactly one version and the vendor's published digest. tests/check_tool_pins_single_version.py refuses any other version or digest of a tool named here anywhere in the kit's code (workflows, composites, scripts, tools, templates, tests). Workflows and composites still carry the literal (a reusable workflow runs in the consumer's checkout, where this file is not), so a bump is: change this file, change every literal the check names, re-run the proofs. Language runtimes a caller chooses (python, go, node, java, dotnet versions) are inputs, not pins, and are not listed.",
  "_exceptions": "An exception is a second version of a tool that something else REQUIRES, scoped to the files named, with the reason. It is never a way to keep an old pin.",
